sis","dsc":0,"cul":1,"persistent":false,"epmc_pair":17,"lift":1.47,"evidence_tier":"studied"},{"concept_id":"hemorrhage","dsc":0,"cul":1,"persistent":false,"epmc_pair":3,"lift":0.05,"evidence_tier":"sparse"},{"concept_id":"inflammation","dsc":0,"cul":1,"persistent":false,"epmc_pair":635,"lift":4.74,"evidence_tier":"studied"},{"concept_id":"jaundice","dsc":0,"cul":1,"persistent":false,"epmc_pair":3,"lift":0.33,"evidence_tier":"sparse"},{"concept_id":"liver_disease","dsc":0,"cul":1,"persistent":false,"epmc_pair":44,"lift":0.75,"evidence_tier":"studied"},{"concept_id":"pain","dsc":1,"cul":0,"persistent":false,"epmc_pair":462,"lift":3.69,"evidence_tier":"studied"},{"concept_id":"sciatica","dsc":0,"cul":1,"persistent":false,"epmc_pair":14,"lift":2.63,"evidence_tier":"studied"},{"concept_id":"sexual_function","dsc":1,"cul":0,"persistent":false,"epmc_pair":3,"lift":0.53,"evidence_tier":"sparse"}],"lead_score":0.725},"texts":{"dsc:3.148":{"ref":"De materia medica 3.148","headword":"κάνναβις","lang":"grc","source":"dioscorides","text":"κάνναβις· φυτὸν εὔχρηστον τῳ βίῳ πρὸς τὰς τῶν εὐτονωτάτων σχοινίων πλοκάς. φύλλα δὲ φέρει παραπλήσια τῇ μελίᾳ, δυσώδη, καυλούς μακρούς, κενούς, καρπὸν στρογγύλον, ἐσθιόμενον, ὃς πλείων βρω θεὶς σβέννυσι γονήν· χλωρὸς δὲ χυλισθεὶς ἁρμόζει πρὸς τὰς τῶν ὤτων ἀλγηδόνας ἐνσταζόμενος.","spans":[{"start":203,"end":208,"concept_id":"sexual_function","polarity":"action"},{"start":251,"end":255,"concept_id":"ear_disease","polarity":"therapeutic"},{"start":256,"end":263,"concept_id":"pain","polarity":"therapeutic"}]},"cul:153-hemp":{"ref":"Culpeper, Complete Herbal: Hemp","headword":"Hemp","lang":"en","source":"culpeper","text":"It is a plant of Saturn, and good for something else, you see, than to make halters only. The seed of Hemp consumes wind, and by too much use thereof disperses it so much that it dries up the natural seed for procreation; yet, being boiled in milk and taken, helps such as have a hot dry cough. The Dutch make an emulsion out of the seed, and give it with good success to those that have the jaundice, especially in the beginning of the disease, if there be no ague accompanying it, for it opens obstructions of the gall, and causes digestion of choler. The emulsion or decoction of the seed stays lasks and continual fluxes, eases the cholic, and allays the troublesome humours in the bowels, and stays bleeding at the mouth, nose, or other places, some of the leaves being fried with the blood of them that bleed, and so given them to eat. It is held very good to kill the worms in men or beasts; and the juice dropped into the ears kills worms in them; and draws forth earwigs, or other living creatures gotten into them. The decoction of the root allays inflammations of the head, or any other parts: the herb itself, or the distilled water thereof doth the like. The decoction of the root eases the pains of the gout, the hard humours of knots in the joints, the pains and shrinking of the sinews, and the pains of the hips. The fresh juice mixed with a little oil and butter, is good for any place that hath been burnt with fire, being thereto applied.","spans":[{"start":107,"end":120,"concept_id":"flatulence","polarity":"action"},{"start":179,"end":204,"concept_id":"sexual_function","polarity":"adverse"},{"start":288,"end":293,"concept_id":"cough","polarity":"therapeutic"},{"start":392,"end":400,"concept_id":"jaundice","polarity":"therapeutic"},{"start":461,"end":465,"concept_id":"fever","polarity":"therapeutic"},{"start":496,"end":520,"concept_id":"liver_disease","polarity":"therapeutic"},{"start":533,"end":542,"concept_id":"dyspepsia","polarity":"therapeutic"},{"start":598,"end":603,"concept_id":"diarrhea","polarity":"therapeutic"},{"start":636,"end":642,"concept_id":"colic","polarity":"therapeutic"},{"start":704,"end":712,"concept_id":"hemorrhage","polarity":"therapeutic"},{"start":875,"end":880,"concept_id":"helminthiasis","polarity":"therapeutic"},{"start":921,"end":946,"concept_id":"ear_disease","polarity":"therapeutic"},{"start":972,"end":979,"concept_id":"ear_disease","polarity":"therapeutic"},{"start":1058,"end":1071,"concept_id":"inflammation","polarity":"therapeutic"},{"start":1217,"end":1221,"concept_id":"gout","polarity":"therapeutic"},{"start":1278,"end":1301,"concept_id":"convulsions","polarity":"therapeutic"},{"start":1311,"end":1328,"concept_id":"sciatica","polarity":"therapeutic"},{"start":1419,"end":1434,"concept_id":"burns","polarity":"therapeutic"}]}},"gloss":{"dsc:3.148":{"203":"semen (γονή)","251":"the ears (ὦτα)","256":"pain (ἀλγηδών)"},"cul:153-hemp":{"107":"expels / breaks wind (carminative)","179":"dries up the natural seed; spoils the spirit procreative","288":"cough, coughs","392":"yellow jaundice, black jaundice","461":"agues: intermittent fevers","496":"obstructions of the gall","533":"digestion / indigestion","598":"lask: diarrhoea, looseness of the bowels","636":"cholic: colic, griping abdominal pain","704":"bleeding (inward / outward / of wounds)","875":"worms (intestinal)","921":"dropped into the ears, eases the pains / kills the worms","972":"imposthumed / running ears; earwigs; decayed hearing","1058":"inflammations","1217":"gout","1278":"shrinking of the sinews: contracture","1311":"pains of the hips / huckle-bone","1419":"burnt with fire / gunpowder"}},"images":["cannabissativadior"]}